      "side": 1,
      "message": "Logically this makes no sense -- you have a missing battery, yet the battery isn\u0027t SW-disconnected and has a sufficient charge.\n\nbattery_get_disconnect_state() mostly means \"can the battery actually provide the charge it claims\" (maybe we can comment the prototype to make it more clear), so it might make more sense to have battery_get_disconnect_state() return the appropriate value when the battery is in the state you mentioned in the commit message.",
